{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/972455-thinking-about-how-to-update-inferno","id":972455,"title":"Thinking about how to update Inferno","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-19T05:10:38-07:00","id":972455,"title":"Thinking about how to update Inferno","content":"I've been reading that book again, and I remembered how much I liked it. Yes, the book could have stood to focus on the Inferno itself a little more (just because Hell is ultimately humanity's conspirator doesn't mean it isn't that interesting-Ars Magica's take on the Infernal comes to mind), but Indebted were awesome, Possessed almost as much (because derangement enhancers were always a little too specific to be good).<br /> <br /> So I was thinking-how do I bring the book into 2E, beyond the projects I've already seen?<br /> <br /> The fluff comes first-to go with 2E's more amoral world, I was thinking the Inferno isn't really just evil because they are (driven by Vice, but to-ma-to, to-mah-to), but to make the fact that their Hell is part of, or a function of, the Lower Depths-demons are always lacking <i>something</i>, and they are driven by their desperate hunger for whatever it is they feel they need. Their Testaments are expressions of this hunger-they literally devour and absorb the lore about them they find palatable, changing and evolving to fit the form they were given. This is also about the only way you can deal with them and come out even where you started-you have to keep the deal squarely in the area of &quot;if you change this, you will lose access to what you want&quot; for demons; otherwise, yes, they do betray the spirit on a whim. They can't help but take as much as they possibly can, including power in a working relationship.<br /> <br /> Also, Whisperers-the core idea is good, but they need easier ways of Minor Shaping (waiting for an Integrity roll before it can do anything to communicate in a way other than schizophrenia-voice is boring) and rules for what they do when not attached to someone. Allows greater flexibility and more paranoia. And their relationship with the playable kind of demon (I like the idea that God-Machine angels can't become Diaboli, as they have free will, just obscured...but the Inferno likes to claim Unchained are actually the loyalists' corrupted version, partially out of actual belief, mostly because it lulls Unchained into a false sense of security the Unclean can exploit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T05:49:02-07:00","id":972463,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest creating an infernal template for Ghosts, Spirits, and Goetics simular to what Abyssal beings get.<br /> <br /> For Dominions I'd use the Horror rules with Dread Powers.<br /> <br /> The Possessed, I'd make them a major template instead of a minor one. Vice becomes their power stat and their former vice and virtue are lost in exchange for the Demons Malpraxis.<br /> <br /> Sins, the powers would be organized by the traditional seven deadly sins and dot rating, with a 1 experience point per dot cost like Changeling contracts.<br /> <br /> The Possessed stop aging, gain the ability to speak in tongues, lie perfectly, and a sense vice ability.<br /> <br /> I'd replace Burnout with Desacrate now that Burnout is accoiciated with Deviants now.<br /> <br /> And I'd call all these beings devils instead of demons so as not to have it confused with well Demons of the Godmachine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T05:52:11-07:00","id":972465,"title":"","content":"&quot;So I was thinking-how do I bring the book into 2E, beyond the projects I've already seen?&quot;<br /> <br /> So, we start with the standard questions for this topic.<br /> 1. Are you intending on keeping the 7 Deadly Sins theme? That's no longer a thing in the CofD by nature, so you'd need to build that from the ground up unique to the Inferno.<br /> 2. How are you going to define &quot;evil&quot; with the changes to Integrity from Morality? The Inferno needs to feed on something like sin - what metric are you using? How do you intend on avoiding the whole association of mental imbalance = evil theme of the old game?<br /> 3. Whisperers basically act like goetics. Are you going to establish a difference? Because, as things stand, there's no meaningful difference. While on the matter, what would these creatures be &quot;lacking&quot; that makes them different from existing ephemerals? The answer for strix and the Lifeless is obviously life essence. <br /> 4. Relationship to the Lucifuge? Belial's Brood and Maeljin? Beasts?<br /> 5. You already mentioned angels, but you haven't discussed the Exiled (DtD's equivalent to fallen's Earthbound demons). How about things like strix, fae (and Fae) and qashmal? <br /> 6. How will you integrate Social Maneuvering and Investigation subsystems? Specifically, in relationship to the Possessed dealing with their inner demon (ha!) and summoning rituals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:38:14-07:00","id":972516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/972455-thinking-about-how-to-update-inferno?p=972465#post972465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;So I was thinking-how do I bring the book into 2E, beyond the projects I've already seen?&quot;<br /> <br /> So, we start with the standard questions for this topic.<br /> 1. Are you intending on keeping the 7 Deadly Sins theme? That's no longer a thing in the CofD by nature, so you'd need to build that from the ground up unique to the Inferno.<br /> 2. How are you going to define &quot;evil&quot; with the changes to Integrity from Morality? The Inferno needs to feed on something like sin - what metric are you using? How do you intend on avoiding the whole association of mental imbalance = evil theme of the old game?<br /> 3. Whisperers basically act like goetics. Are you going to establish a difference? Because, as things stand, there's no meaningful difference. While on the matter, what would these creatures be &quot;lacking&quot; that makes them different from existing ephemerals? The answer for strix and the Lifeless is obviously life essence.<br /> 4. Relationship to the Lucifuge? Belial's Brood and Maeljin? Beasts?<br /> 5. You already mentioned angels, but you haven't discussed the Exiled (DtD's equivalent to fallen's Earthbound demons). How about things like strix, fae (and Fae) and qashmal?<br /> 6. How will you integrate Social Maneuvering and Investigation subsystems? Specifically, in relationship to the Possessed dealing with their inner demon (ha!) and summoning rituals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideas (even if I'm not the exact one being addressed):<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Base it on a general theme of &quot;Corruption&quot; or &quot;Pure Selfishness&quot;?</li> <li>There are a few Breaking Point triggers that are based off the idea of &quot;transgression&quot;, like Murder, etc. Use those? Perhaps Infernals don't care so much about &quot;Sin&quot;, as chipping away pieces of other's souls (represented through Integrity loss)? Mental Imbalance might make things easier, but it is just a side thing, really.</li> <li>They might lack the full suite of Ephemeral abilities? Rank, Attributes, Essence, Numina, Manifestations, etc.</li> <li>&lt;shrug&gt; The world is mysterious. There is some link, in some cases, and no link in others? Be vague, but suggestive?</li> <li>If it is an Ephemeral-only template, the others wouldn't be susceptable anyways, not being Ephemeral. As for Exiles... Corruption -&gt; Fall -&gt; no-Longer Ephemeral? Or the God-Machine still has enough oversight on the Exile to lock out the intruder?</li> <li>Summoning could use the core Research and Summon rules? Social Maneuvering against the Infernal might be a nice touch.</li> </ol>As far as powersets go, what about using the 7 Sins as an example (with maybe one more to show the mold can be broken)? Just say Infernal powers are many and varied, and the ones listed are only a sample?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:22:23-07:00","id":972536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/972455-thinking-about-how-to-update-inferno?p=972465#post972465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;So I was thinking-how do I bring the book into 2E, beyond the projects I've already seen?&quot;<br /> <br /> So, we start with the standard questions for this topic.<br /> 1. Are you intending on keeping the 7 Deadly Sins theme? That's no longer a thing in the CofD by nature, so you'd need to build that from the ground up unique to the Inferno.<br /> <br /> <b>If I am, it's only as Possessed power classifications, and I'll imply it's because the 7 Deadlies are so ingrained to modern consciencess that it's influenced the ever-malleable Inferno. I'm more aiming for the theme being one of desire and hunger-how they both drive and destroy.</b><br /> <br /> 2. How are you going to define &quot;evil&quot; with the changes to Integrity from Morality? The Inferno needs to feed on something like sin - what metric are you using? How do you intend on avoiding the whole association of mental imbalance = evil theme of the old game?<br /> <br /> <b>Here's my big twist-embracing the Inferno actually <i><u>cements</u> </i>Integrity, if you aren't killed or driven nuts by diabolic mind rape before you get experienced. Real evil requires intent and will, and that's a function of a stable mind and strength of will. Thus, the deeper a true diabolist sinks, her patrons guarantee that she will be cold enough to ignore the consequences that might cause a Guilty condition in the future, and if so, she resolves it by denying she ever felt bad in the first place. The idea is that an act of true malice gets a bonus to the Integrity roll, as the ego is actually confirmed by the will to do this thing and not feel regret. Succeeding in the roll grants something like a Hubristic or Zealous condition, as the person either revels in invulnerability or the self-righteousness of the action, and the devils (thank you, Omega) egg her on. This also means diabolists come off as being very coldly rational-just as the deepest level of Hell is ice, so to is the fully initiated malificar's heart, chilled and relentless. </b><br /> <br /> 3. Whisperers basically act like goetics. Are you going to establish a difference? Because, as things stand, there's no meaningful difference. While on the matter, what would these creatures be &quot;lacking&quot; that makes them different from existing ephemerals? The answer for strix and the Lifeless is obviously life essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Form. Identity. Really, the self-ironic, given how selfish they are. They exist largely in relationship to what they can grant, what they know, and what they want-nothing about what they <u><i>are.</i></u> And they <i><u>hate it</u>.</i> Hence, Testaments-by describing the devil, you define the devil, and in the process, give him an answer to the question &quot;Who am I?&quot; Whisperers can be considered a devil's truest state, in this case-once in that state, they become little more than their own actions on their host and whatever area they've nested in, living coincidences and inspiration with a thought process. They're different from goetics in that goetics actually do have a true form-an intangible one made of astral energy, but its theirs. Devils don't even have that, naturally.</b><br /> <br /> 4. Relationship to the Lucifuge? Belial's Brood and Maeljin? Beasts?<br /> <br /> <b>Keeping it vague, just as in the book. Beasts probably do have a kinship, though-but not to Whisperers, as once again, a Whisperer is more the quality that makes a being Kin rather than Kin itself. Results in some interesting effects when the Begotten discover a Whisperer-possessed.</b><br /> <br /> 5. You already mentioned angels, but you haven't discussed the Exiled (DtD's equivalent to fallen's Earthbound demons). How about things like strix, fae (and Fae) and qashmal?<br /> <br /> <b>Like in the original, True Fae and qashmal are too important to reality to be possessed-but I'm thinking about giving them to Diabolize particularly wicked Hedge Beasts and oneiroi (in fact, it could be said that the Succubi changelings are familiar with are Diaboli fae). Strix are explicitly from the Lower Depths already, so they can't be Diabolized for the same reason you can't fall off the floor. Exiles, though...Exiles are something special. After all, they're angels too-but with Abandonment comes <u><i>wanting things</i></u> like a new mission, or to return to God. And the devils hear that... </b><br /> <br /> 6. How will you integrate Social Maneuvering and Investigation subsystems? Specifically, in relationship to the Possessed dealing with their inner demon (ha!) and summoning rituals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't decided. Probably the internal debate between Possessed and soul-buddy deserves a subset of that for coaxing extra power in return for favors out, and summoning rituals...can be ported to Investigation as is, with special Botch mechanics for being swindled by cults looking to sacrifice stupid diabolists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:54:55-07:00","id":972553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/972455-thinking-about-how-to-update-inferno#post972455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fluff comes first-to go with 2E's more amoral world, I was thinking the Inferno isn't really just evil because they are (driven by Vice, but to-ma-to, to-mah-to), but to make the fact that their Hell is part of, or a function of, the Lower Depths-demons are always lacking <i>something</i>, and they are driven by their desperate hunger for whatever it is they feel they need.</div> </div> </div> </div>DaveB has outright said that's what they are, so you can use that with abandon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If there's a corresponding Empyrean, I'd make it also a Lower Depth, just driven by a different lack and a different hunger. And only enemies when they run into each other and spoil each other's food.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their Testaments are expressions of this hunger-they literally devour and absorb the lore about them they find palatable, changing and evolving to fit the form they were given. </div> </div> </div>Things of the Lower Depths are only half-real, the definition inherent in a Testament gives them more reality - they need it as much as they need sin (and find the two easy to mesh together).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Whisperers-the core idea is good, but they need easier ways of Minor Shaping (waiting for an Integrity roll before it can do anything to communicate in a way other than schizophrenia-voice is boring) and rules for what they do when not attached to someone. Allows greater flexibility and more paranoia. </div> </div> </div>I can't recall off the top of my head, but are Whisperers (which I think would be creepier if just called Whispers) able to attach to objects or places as well as people? If not, change that.<br /> <br /> Suggestions for some of MCN's questions:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/972455-thinking-about-how-to-update-inferno?p=972465#post972465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;So I was thinking-how do I bring the book into 2E, beyond the projects I've already seen?&quot;<br /> <br /> So, we start with the standard questions for this topic.<br /> 1. Are you intending on keeping the 7 Deadly Sins theme? That's no longer a thing in the CofD by nature, so you'd need to build that from the ground up unique to the Inferno.<br /> 2. How are you going to define &quot;evil&quot; with the changes to Integrity from Morality? The Inferno needs to feed on something like sin - what metric are you using? How do you intend on avoiding the whole association of mental imbalance = evil theme of the old game?<br /> 3. Whisperers basically act like goetics. Are you going to establish a difference? Because, as things stand, there's no meaningful difference. While on the matter, what would these creatures be &quot;lacking&quot; that makes them different from existing ephemerals? The answer for strix and the Lifeless is obviously life essence.<br /> 4. Relationship to the Lucifuge? Belial's Brood and Maeljin? Beasts?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Make the Inferno itself a fourth &quot;layer&quot; over Whisperers, Diaboli, and Dominions, in some ways an entity in itself. The seven deadlies, and any similar schema you feel like bringing in are part of <i>its</i> Testament, and other demons are stuck with it. This means that part and parcel of setting up a demonic pact is warping your vice (or even your virtue if the demon is having a lucky day) so that it fits into that pattern.<br /> <br /> 2. I like your idea.<br /> <br /> 3. Your answer squares with what I said about Testaments.<br /> [Come to think of it, you could replace sin with need: what does the pacter need so much they'll abandon everything else for? That's what the demon provides, and in return gets the definition as something that can provide it, and the consequent sense of reality. Sin's only relevant inasmuch as &quot;abandoning everything else&quot; is likely to include a lot of things that would come under the category of evil, or at least be interpreted as such, but what the demon is really after is desperation. That doesn't really square with your idea about cementing Integrity, though; it's more like a way to reconcile the mental balance and evil approaches to looking at the score]<br /> <br /> 4. Between Inferno and Spirit Slayers, the Maeljin are explicitly Inferno demons, and Lucifuge are explicitly the descendants of Inferno demons. Everything about their theme and tone match up too well to be coy about it. Keep the connection, anything else is dilution. However, remember what I suggested about the Inferno itself kind of being an entity? <i>That's</i> the Lucifuges' ancestor, not a regular demon, even a dominion. And that's why their blood s &quot;royal.&quot;<br /> In the same vein, make Belial's Brood and the Bale Hounds infernalists. Not the Dark Mother, though; primordial terror and chaos isn't quite the same as the desperate sin and yearning demons peddle in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T09:07:55-07:00","id":972559,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but I don't understand the answer to the second question - How are you determining &quot;acts of evil?&quot; It seems like you kind of got onto a whole &quot;diabolists don't lose Integrity here&quot; which is fair enough, but it still doesn't touch on how demons are going to be feeding, or on what. <br /> <br /> On the third question, I don't see how that explains what they're lacking to be a lower-depth thing. Their &quot;lack&quot; drives them to feed on others. If they lack an identity, and get one through testaments and the like... then what point is there to come back? What happens when a benevolant identity is given? That's not very demonic. What about infected goetics, ghosts and spirits? They HAVE an identity. What is desirable about being a demon if it means losing that identity? <br /> <br /> <br /> These two are kind of interrelated. You have a theme of desire/hunger you want to push, but there's little explanation about how you're going about feeding that desire, or what constittues feeding. And the identity aspect that you claim they lack doesn't really relate to themes of desire or hunger. It doesn't really seem to relate to each other. <br /> <br /> The remade 2e games start out their books with listing themes, usually three. So, what are your three themes here? Desire is Sacred, All Identities are Defined By Others and....? Anything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T10:33:44-07:00","id":972592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/972455-thinking-about-how-to-update-inferno?p=972559#post972559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when a benevolant identity is given? That's not very demonic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we get an Empyreal angel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about infected goetics, ghosts and spirits? They HAVE an identity. What is desirable about being a demon if it means losing that identity? </div> </div> </div>That assumes that becoming a demon is voluntary - which, in fairness, it ought to be. The only feasible answer is power, in a parallel to the makers of a pact eventually being driven to give up everything about themselves except what they made the pact to satisfy. Perhaps in this case, Diaboli are actually spirits that have made a pact for some reason rather than a type of demon as such. Or maybe eliminate the part about other ephemerals becoming demons, but allow demons to disguise themselves as such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These two are kind of interrelated. You have a theme of desire/hunger you want to push, but there's little explanation about how you're going about feeding that desire, or what constittues feeding. And the identity aspect that you claim they lack doesn't really relate to themes of desire or hunger. It doesn't really seem to relate to each other. </div> </div> </div>What if they only react to one another accidentally, as it were. The demons hunger for definition, but that definition can only be provided by the desperate - only that has the requisite level of spiritual energy invested in it (like the Divine Fire in that respect). Desperation leads people to be their best and worst selves, so its that best and worst they want satisfied in return for the definition they offer. Worst in the case of demons - and it knocks on, in that definition will make the demon better at satisfying that kind of worst self.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The remade 2e games start out their books with listing themes, usually three. So, what are your three themes here? Desire is Sacred, All Identities are Defined By Others and....? Anything else? </div> </div> </div>My lastmost suggestion could suggest evil begets evil.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:13:18-07:00","id":972707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/972455-thinking-about-how-to-update-inferno?p=972559#post972559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but I don't understand the answer to the second question - How are you determining &quot;acts of evil?&quot; It seems like you kind of got onto a whole &quot;diabolists don't lose Integrity here&quot; which is fair enough, but it still doesn't touch on how demons are going to be feeding, or on what.<br /> <br /> <b>Well, that's because I forgot to answer that half of the question, so oops. I will say Inferno has a pretty good definition for an evil act-an intentional, avoidable act motivated at least in part by malice that the perpetrator knows will hurt another person in an extreme way, but refuses to care about except on purely pragmatic levels. Hence the idea it actually cements Integrity for true adherents of malifica-thinking and behaving in that cold a way is going to leave someone a very cold, very heartless-and thus, very focused-fish. </b><br /> <br /> On the third question, I don't see how that explains what they're lacking to be a lower-depth thing. Their &quot;lack&quot; drives them to feed on others. If they lack an identity, and get one through testaments and the like... then what point is there to come back? What happens when a benevolant identity is given? That's not very demonic. What about infected goetics, ghosts and spirits? They HAVE an identity. What is desirable about being a demon if it means losing that identity?<br /> <br /> <b>Nick actually brought up a good idea-many Diaboli chose to be that way for the promise of infernal power as a Dominion or just for that nifty Hellform (yes, it devours their own self sooner or later, but that's also in-theme with the self-destructive nature of Hell). Some, however, aren't actually the original beings at all, but were eaten from the inside out by a Whisper being fed by the spiritual darkness of a place or action like a virus, replacing the ephemeral's essence with itself. And some were just born that way-the worst Wound spirits come to mind. As for benevolent identities, well, Nick pointed out one solution, but here's where Ars Magica shows its influence-there is such a thing as a Devil of Virtue, they just don't look it, and they don't think they are. They're what the book called Nemeses, but what in Ars Magica would be called Avengers of Evil, or Accusers-devils who look like and think they are angels, acting to punish the actions inspired by devils who look it. Avengers especially, since it's explicit that when they're involved, they end up actually <u>making things worse</u> a lot of the time, as they end up having a far too strict interpretation of good and drive the guilty to think they're irredeemable, driving them further into darkness.</b><br /> <br /> These two are kind of interrelated. You have a theme of desire/hunger you want to push, but there's little explanation about how you're going about feeding that desire, or what constittues feeding. And the identity aspect that you claim they lack doesn't really relate to themes of desire or hunger. It doesn't really seem to relate to each other.<br /> <br /> The remade 2e games start out their books with listing themes, usually three. So, what are your three themes here? Desire is Sacred, All Identities are Defined By Others and....? Anything else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I skipped that. Mostly because the system of Malapraxis, as is, isn't in need of too much altering-I just need to give it more than seven Vices to work with, and a system for feeding on non-Malapraxis acts. <br /> <br /> The three themes would be as you both say, just a little twist: Double Edged Desire, Identities Are Defined by Others, and Darkness Feeds Itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T05:59:24-07:00","id":973069,"title":"","content":"I think I have to fundamentally disagree with the idea of being able to choose your own identity for becoming something that could be less-than-evil here, so I'm bowing out of this conversation. Good bye and good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:56:04-07:00","id":973496,"title":"","content":"<b>&quot;Here's my big twist-embracing the Inferno actually <i><u>cements</u> </i>Integrity, if you aren't killed or driven nuts by diabolic mind rape before you get experienced. Real evil requires intent and will, and that's a function of a stable mind and strength of will. Thus, the deeper a true diabolist sinks, her patrons guarantee that she will be cold enough to ignore the consequences that might cause a Guilty condition in the future, and if so, she resolves it by denying she ever felt bad in the first place. The idea is that an act of true malice gets a bonus to the Integrity roll, as the ego is actually confirmed by the will to do this thing and not feel regret. Succeeding in the roll grants something like a Hubristic or Zealous condition, as the person either revels in invulnerability or the self-righteousness of the action, and the devils (thank you, Omega) egg her on. This also means diabolists come off as being very coldly rational-just as the deepest level of Hell is ice, so to is the fully initiated malificar's heart, chilled and relentless. </b>&quot;<br /> <br /> I have to admit, I really like the ideas behind this part. Especially given how Integrity is less like Morality in terms that it covers Sanity as opposed to Morality. Keep up the awesome train of thought, Lel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T16:19:28-07:00","id":976786,"title":"","content":"I'll point out that Inferno demons are vice driven, but they're not straight up evil, they're not that straight forward.<br /> <br /> And Empyreans are about virtue, but not good, and in fact it makes it pretty clear that being posssessed by an Empyrean is usually straight up worse then most Infernal possessions, because devils of the Inferno are self interest driven and you can really get much out of someone who've ruined or killed, but a &quot;selfless&quot; Empyrean has no such restraints, which can mean ruining or killing the host in the pursuit of a &quot;greater good&quot;.<br /> <br /> So on the surface its black and white morality, but when you look deeper and realize they're both Lower Depths entities, not truely biblical beings (although they may in some cases have inspired such beings), its starts to become clear that they're are shades of grey and even blue orange morality invovled.<br /> <br /> These beings, devils and empyreans, are victims of bad luck, they were born or assimulated in the lower depths, different lower depths, but still empty of some trait which they are driven to hunger for.<br /> <br /> I'm point out that if Demons hunger for vice, it ironically means the Inferno likely lacks pleasure/vice and the Enpyrean heaven lacks in true virtue/suffering, in otherwords no one suffers in heaven so virtue is meaningless and serves no purpose, no one is pushed towards vice, and in the inferno everything is suffering, nothing is enjoyable, so indulging yourself is pointless, which makes vice pointless.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Faith is belief in the right things (including the virtues!)&quot; You don't need Faith in Heaven, your in heaven.<br /> <br /> Hope is taking a positive future view, that good will prevail. You don't need Hope, because in Heaven there is no reason to ever fear you will suffer, because there is no suffering.<br /> <br /> Charity is concern for, and active helping of, others. In Heaven no one needs your Charity.<br /> <br /> Fortitude is never giving up. You don't need Fortitude because there is no suffering to challenge it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Justice is being fair and equitable with others.&quot; In Heaven there is no crime, so what do you need with justice.<br /> <br /> &quot;Prudence is care of and moderation with money.&quot; What need do you have for money, wgen in Heaven where all your needs are met, therefor Prudence isn't needed either nor do you need to be careful, heaven has no sharp edges, or,at least none that can harm you, those could cause suffering.<br /> <br /> &quot;Temperance is moderation of needed things and abstinence from things which are not needed &quot; Temperance is not needed in Heaven because there is no suffering, therefor there are no consquences to over indulgence.<br /> <br /> And the same is true in reverse for vices.<br /> <br /> Lust is pointless if you can't enjoy sex in the Inferno.<br /> <br /> Greed is pointless if there is nothing in the Inferno worth having.<br /> <br /> Envy is pointless if all anyone has is suffering, which in the Inferno you already have in abundence.<br /> <br /> Sloth is pointless when anything other then escaping isn't worth doing anyways.<br /> <br /> Wrath is pointless when anyone you'd be pissed off at is already suffering, its redundant.<br /> <br /> Pride is pointless when there is nothing in the Inferno worth having Pride in.<br /> <br /> Gluttony is pointless when everything tastes like shit and nothing you eat is filling in the Inferno.<br /> <br /> So Empyreans go out in search of the virtue that they can't find in the paradise of Heaven and the Devils go out in search of the vice they can't find in the Inferno.<br /> <br /> So its not as straight up good and evil, instead its about finally being able feed the empty space inside you for the first time ever and that is something the devils and empyreans oddly have in common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T05:05:06-07:00","id":977692,"title":"","content":"Nice. Very good points Omega.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:26:57-07:00","id":978028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/972455-thinking-about-how-to-update-inferno?p=977692#post977692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. Very good points Omega.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:06:08-07:00","id":978854,"title":"","content":"The latest episode of Darker Days Podcast actually talks about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T23:34:44-07:00","id":978891,"title":"","content":"I just point to my take on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978886-inferno-2e-based-on-integrity\">Inferno 2E update, based on Vice and Integrity rules</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978886-inferno-2e-based-on-integrity#post978886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I initially presented </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">my</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> idea</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">s</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> for </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Inferno </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">rulebook update</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> to 2E in this topic. </span></span><span style=\"color:#0563C1\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-update-ideas</a></u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">discussion</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> is dedicated to a specific mechanics</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> I envision</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">. If you do not agree with my assumptions - better to </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">not</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> writing in it</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> and go somewhere else.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">You stayed? Okay, here is rough draft.</span> I took idea on Conditions and demon evolution from <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/\" target=\"_blank\">Charlaquin</a> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">post in original topic.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2022 <i>Hearing Whispers </i>is a Persistent Condition that characters can gain instead of the normal Persistent Conditions for Dramatic Failure on Integrity Breaking Point if that Breaking Point played into their Vice.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2022 When a character with the <i>Hearing Whispers</i> Condition interacts with an ephemeral entity via the &quot;Interactions with Mortals&quot; or targets one with a supernatural power, there is a chance the mortal will lose the Condition and transfer it to the ephemeral entity.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Truth about Inferno</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Hell is dimension</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> outside of normal reality that mages describe as one of </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Lower </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Depths. </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">It\u2019s fueled by Sin \u2013 that in mechanics way is understood as Vice related Breaking Points</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">, in which </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">act of </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Breaking Point marks \u2018</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">wickedness</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2019</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">. What\u2019s interesting, Breaking Points do not need to stir from humans Integrity \u2013 Humanity, </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Harmony or Wisdom are all good </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">food for Inferno demons.</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Hell\u2019s servants feed on depraving and breaking people \u2013 supernatural or normal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Demons spread by Sin \u2013 when </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">someone is under Breaking Point based on Vice, he can start to hear Whisperer instead of other Dramatic </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Failure</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> effects</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> on roll.</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> He </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Hearing Whisperer</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Condition</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> (see below)</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Diaboli</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> are created by Ephemeral Beings interactions with Whisperers in others \u2013 or </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">by some vile</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> ways of Inferno </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">entering our world </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">itself. Some say that really wicked ghosts can become </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Larvals </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">or that Sin polluted spirits can transform in to </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Immundi</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">. Astral Realms are hosting </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Deceptors </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">from </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">g</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">oetia</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> of</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> those people that were infected with Whisperers. </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">S</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">upposedly there are other methods </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">to corrupt </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">e</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">phemera</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">l beings.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><i>Hearing Whisperer</i> ( </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Persistent</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>, Vice )</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Your character is </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">hearing from time to time little voice in his head that leads him to commit sins. </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">By listening to those </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">thoughts</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">, she can rebuild her Willpower. </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Character a</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">cts</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> as having second Vice decided when </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">acquiring this Condition. If Vice of Whisperer is the same as characters original, </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">it </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> her two Willpower points instead of one when </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">fulfilling</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> it. </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">However, r</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">eal reward is in</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> breaking Integrity ( or </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">it\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> equivalent ) in light of Sins \u2013 if character leads or is under Breaking Point based on the Vice of Whisperer, she regains number of Willpower points equal to cumulative negative penalties of the act.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Resolution:</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Exorcism</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> of Whisperer. Mental </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">therapy</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">.</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Passing Whisperer to Ephemeral Being by contact with it</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> as per </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Mortal Interactions</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> rules in </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>CoD</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b> Rulebook</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Beat:</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Your character chooses to </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">make act leading to Breaking Point based on Vice</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">.</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Confronting Ephemeral Being to pass the Whisperer to it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><b><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Inferno Demon Template</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">All Hell\u2019s demons are previous </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">E</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">phemeral </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">B</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">eings of other kinds \u2013 ghosts,</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> spirits or </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">goetia</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">. ( Other </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">beings maybe also can be remade in to demons. ) Being then </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Inferno Demon Template on top of </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">it\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> original one, so </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Larvals</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> are still</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> and work under rules as</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> ghosts with Inferno Demon Template.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">New traits and rules for Inferno Demon:</span></span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Being </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Vice trait, even if not having it previously.</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> This Vice works as one for the ghosts.</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> If it did have other Vice before, Vice is switched to the one coming from transformation in to </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Hell\u2019s </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">demon.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Being </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> new Influence based on </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">it\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Vice nature</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">, called by demonologist as Key. This Key starts at Beings now Rank.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If Being have Integrity</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> score</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> or </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">it\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">equivalent \u2013 she lose it in transformation.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Being new ways of generating Essence is making acts of Sin. She does not need to do it oneself. </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">It\u2019s even </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">advisable</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> that others should do those action in her place. If she makes acts of Sin, she </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> back her Rank in Essence. If she make </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>other</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">character </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">to do those</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">, </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">she also </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> bonus Essence</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> points</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> in </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">number of negative penalties character got on her Breaking Points roll.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-30-2016, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:17:33-07:00","id":979034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowlost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/972455-thinking-about-how-to-update-inferno?p=978854#post978854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latest episode of Darker Days Podcast actually talks about this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can I have a link?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:55:06-07:00","id":979465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/972455-thinking-about-how-to-update-inferno?p=979034#post979034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Can I have a link?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://networkzero.podbean.com/e/network-zero-3/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://d8g345wuhgd7e.cloudfront.net/site/images/logo-img2.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://networkzero.podbean.com/e/network-zero-3/\" target=\"_blank\"> Login to your Podbean Account | Podbean </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://networkzero.podbean.com/e/network-zero-3/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://networkzero.podbean.com/e/network-zero-3/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Log into Podbean to start podcasting. Get everything you need for a successful podcast. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T23:57:03-07:00","id":979533,"title":"","content":"Random off the cuff idea about identity and testaments:<br /> <br /> Rolling off of Omega's explanation, if the Inferno is pure suffering, a whisper that is influencing a mortal may implant an experience of the Inferno directly into their mind. Unable to truly comprehend it, the mortal filters these perceptions in a dream-like manner, drawing on their memories, imagination, and cultural symbolism. This is what drives the mortal to describe and define the torment, and the demon to incorporate an identity rooted in &quot;evil&quot; (thus preventing the mortal writing a positive testament).<br /> <br /> It could also apply to defining their malpraxis: after being tormented into defining pure suffering, the mortal would naturally try to escape the feeling by indulging in blind short-term pleasure; which the demon could co-opt as well. There may even be a multi-fetter process where the whisper becomes a true demon one mortal at a time, taking a peice of their identity slowly through a variety of interpretations ....<br /> This may even bridge nicely into Wyrd's idea of breaking integrity via vice causing a whisper to fetter to you - prior to that, the demon has no identity at all, and that occurence leads to their malpraxis, and from there, new possesions and further definition.<br /> <br /> It adds a personalized and subjective approach to the evil and horror to the Inferno, in keeping with CoD, I think, while staying true to its themes.<br /> <br /> But I'm just spit balling here...<br /> <br /> For bonus points, it can be inverted to reflect the Empyrean (formless angel, fetters to a mortal who loses integrity due to their virtue, and floods their mind with experiencing pure... grace? contentment? in order to be defined). Though this results in the equivalent virtuous beings, it does so far more rarely because: 1) dramatically failing a breaking point through a virtue is harder, 2) those visions are more difficult to focus into an entity and an action responsible for them, and 3) in such a cynical setting, more people would imagine the flaws in paradise than would imagine the paragons of good, leading to more dystopia novels than angels - all of which emphasizes how distant and rare truly virtuous beings are in the Chronicles of Darkness (before hitting home it's subversive element of angels craving conflict, sacrifice, and suffering to really embody virtue - as, again, Omega's excellent ideas suggested).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 10-01-2016, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T01:49:19-07:00","id":979555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/972455-thinking-about-how-to-update-inferno?p=979533#post979533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For bonus points, it can be inverted to reflect the Empyrean (formless angel, fetters to a mortal who loses integrity due to their virtue, and floods their mind with experiencing pure... grace? contentment? in order to be defined). Though this results in the equivalent virtuous beings, it does so far more rarely because: 1) dramatically failing a breaking point through a virtue is harder, 2) those visions are more difficult to focus into an entity and an action responsible for them, and 3) in such a cynical setting, more people would imagine the flaws in paradise than would imagine the paragons of good, leading to more dystopia novels than angels - all of which emphasizes how distant and rare truly virtuous beings are in the Chronicles of Darkness (before hitting home it's subversive element of angels craving conflict, sacrifice, and suffering to really embody virtue - as, again, Omega's excellent ideas suggested).</div> </div> </div> </div>Basicly <i>Supernatural</i>'s Demons ( i.e. Inferno ghosts ) and Heaven Angels ( agents of Virtues ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}